WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100 align:start position:0%
 
there was a very very interesting  interview over the weekend on Fox News  Sunday which is Fox News's version of  the sort of Sunday morning political  talk show and Chris Wallace pointed out  to Secretary of State Rex Tillerson  during this interview that the world  community sort of at large is  increasingly concerned with Donald  Trump's seemingly casual or even  accepting attitude towards really  horrific and vile racism and xenophobic  groups and people for example the United  Nations recently condemned Trump for not  condemning racism in the wake of the  charlottesville debacle that took place  during our vacation and Chris Wallace  asked Rex Tillerson does do the values  of President Trump align with what we  consider to be American values and Rex  Tillerson the top diplomat of the United  States said hey Donald Trump speaks only  for himself purely finally and I've got  a little over a minute left the  controversy over the racial protests in  Charlottesville and the president's  response to it has become an  international issue a UN committee this  week criticized the Trump administration  for quote its failure at the highest  political level to unequivocally reject  and condemn the racist violent events  and demonstrations and here was the  president in Phoenix this week talking  more about the media than he was about  the neo-nazis in the Klan here he is the  only people giving a platform to these  hate groups is the media itself in the  fake good does that make it harder for  you to push American values around the  world when some foreign leaders question  the president's values Chris we express  America's values from the State  Department we represent the American  people we represent America's values our  commitment to freedom our commitment to  equal treatment of people the world over  and that message has never changed and  when the president gets into the kind of  controversy he does in the UN Committee  responds the way as it seems to say they  begin to doubt our whether we're living  those values  I don't believe anyone doubts the  American people's values or the  commitment of the American government or  the government's agencies to advancing  those values and defending those values  and the president's values the president  speaks for himself Chris are you  separating yourself from that sir  I've spoken I've made my own comments as  to our values as well in a speech I gave  to the State Department this past week  Wow I just realized by the way that Rex  Tillerson is like a Texas version of  Sean Connery talking about expressing  his values I know this kind of seems  like okay no big deal there's way  crazier stuff going on and that's true  but this is the Secretary of State  saying listen Trump says what he says  I've spoken about my values and he is  clearly distancing himself in the  American people at large from the values  that Trump seems to portray and rightly  so I mean Trump seems to have no real  values to speak of other than cronyism  deranged grandiosity and greed and so  much nonsense has been normalized by  sort of the sheer idiocy of the Trump  administration this could easily get  lost in the mix the Secretary of State  is on national media not acknowledging  that his values are in line with those  of the President of the United States  for whom he works this is a big deal and  I really think that tiller since  comments here were planned out it wasn't  like it was a gaffe or anything that he  accidentally said yeah normally this  would be you know the response would be  some sort of firing or his forced  resignation but I just think that Rex  Tillerson understands that Donald Trump  doesn't really have the political  capital at this point to do that yeah  because he's been firing way too many  people it's like The Apprentice and the  Secretary of State is just such an  important role it's funny how people  that I would never normally agree with  on anything sort of come through his  voices of reason when compared to Donald  Trump like Jim mattis doesn't know  whether this total ban on the  transgender community from the military  makes total sense Wow seems  comparatively reasonable Secretary of  State Tillerson doesn't think an  escalation of megalomaniacs into World  War three v's of either North Korea  situation is a great idea seems kind of  reasonable the  of Overton Window of insanity is moving  under Trump because he's just so out  there on so many issues and it might be  because Tillerson is making his exit  strategy for leaving the White House  soon and as a guy who's been in business  his whole life and now as a diplomat  yeah I mean PR is very important to him  so he can't just tacitly agree with the  comments that Trump made on  charlottesville I don't agree with the  guy on basically any of his politics but  you can't really say Tillerson is not a  careful guy when it comes to what he  says publicly

